<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68445" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοναρχ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουναρχίη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>monarchy, government
				by a single ruler</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1789
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				883
			</span></i> (lyr., pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.82
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαβὼν χώρας παντελῆ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					1163
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ γὰρ κατέστησ᾽
			αὐτὸν</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δῆμον</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς μοναρχίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					352
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ μισόδημε καὶ μοναρχίας ἐραστά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					474
				</span></i>
			; including <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλική</span> and
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυραννική</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				291e
			</span></i>: in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐν ταῖς μ. ὄντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					2.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1311a24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1279a33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1365b37
			</span></i>; of the Roman Dictator, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				37
			</span></i>; <i>supreme command</i>, of a general, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.1.31
			</span></i>.</div>
